From: Michal Gawronski-Kot <michal@gawronskikot.com>
Subject: [PATCH] feat(signal): deliver photos and voice notes to the media pipeline

Local komodo_library patch on top of v0.8.5 (not upstream). The Signal
channel always built ChannelMessage with `attachments: vec![]` and produced
no message at all for a caption-less photo or voice note, so both were
silently dropped. Attachments are now fetched from signal-cli
(`getAttachment`, base64, <=20 MB each) into the first message, and an
attachment-only envelope yields one empty-text message. The orchestrator's
existing [media_pipeline] then inlines images for a vision model and
transcribes audio. Voice notes (audio/aac) are named .m4a because the
transcription path only accepts container extensions.

Also: the local_whisper transcription provider sends the upload as
`audio_file` when its URL path ends in /asr (whisper-asr-webservice) instead
of `file` (whisper.cpp / OpenAI-style).
